id: pm-466m0j
title: "GH-1202: Classify abandoned merge receipts without losing durable provenance"
description: Reproduce receipt lifecycle after an aborted rebase and distinguish an abandoned candidate from a merge requiring review. Current source and Merge Safety documentation intentionally track privacy-safe durable sidecars; raw free-form retained/discarded values are clone-local under .git. Durable receipts retain hashes and only allowlisted low-cardinality scalar previews. The report has not demonstrated a secret leak. A blanket gitignore or evidence deletion would break cross-clone provenance and is not an accepted remedy.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-05T19:06:20.194Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-06T08:26:21.431Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-06T08:26:20.836Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-06T08:26:20.836Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "An actual conflicting rebase followed by abort has deterministic receipt classification and a supported recovery path; Recovery preserves immutable evidence and cannot dismiss an applied merge merely because a later snapshot differs; Fresh-clone tests prove tracked sidecars never contain arbitrary descriptions, acceptance text, or custom status values; CLI guidance clearly distinguishes clone-local raw receipts from intentionally tracked durable sidecars"
value: Reduce recovery ambiguity and preserve trustworthy project context for agents
outcome: A reproducible SDK contract with actionable CLI recovery and regression evidence
why_now: New user report GH-1202 during PR #1204 final integration
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: medium
severity: high
resolution: Capture rebase provenance and settle exact restored-origin receipts with retry-safe immutable audit evidence; revalidate Git proof under the rewrite lock.
expected_result: "Reject changed Git, item or history state without persisting false settlement, while preserving normal and interrupted recovery."
actual_result: Real HEAD and operation-marker lock races reject without item/history/receipt mutation; linked recovery tests and all 8477 tests pass at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. Review and merge remain separate.
affected_version: 2026.9.5
component: sdk/merge
