notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-05T19:06:20.194Z","harness:codex",Reproduce receipt lifecycle after an aborted rebase and distinguish an abandoned candidate from a merge requiring review. Current source and Merge Safety documentation intentionally track privacy-safe durable sidecars; raw free-form retained/discarded values are clone-local under .git. Durable receipts retain hashes and only allowlisted low-cardinality scalar previews. The report has not demonstrated a secret leak. A blanket gitignore or evidence deletion would break cross-clone provenance and is not an accepted remedy.
  "2026-09-06T04:53:19.264Z","harness:codex","Restored-origin settlement preserves durable sidecars and appends an explicit abandoned_receipts audit event. Git original head/blob, clean history, index and working bytes are checked; exact loaded item bytes are revalidated under the existing rewrite snapshot contract. No implicit force or deletion."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-06T05:28:55.800Z","harness:codex","Restored files alone do not prove an aborted Git operation. Capture original commit and blob coordinates during the rebase, then require inactive Git operation markers, matching HEAD, index and working blob, and a clean immutable history snapshot before appending an explicit abandonment audit."
  "2026-09-06T06:08:41.391Z","harness:codex",Clone-local raw receipts belong in Git administrative storage. Tracked .agents/pm/merge-receipts sidecars contain privacy-safe durable provenance and must not be ignored; aborted operations need proven audited settlement rather than deletion.
